  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH Assistance to Conflict Affected IDPs and Refugees in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 12 month proposed water, sanitation and hygiene project is part of a larger emergency response programme whereby
CAFOD and its local partner Catholic Diocese of Tombura-Yambio (CDTY) deliver much needed food, non-food items, basic
shelter, water and sanitation, education and emergency health services for households affected by the continuing LRA crisis
in Western Equatoria State. The programme also provides support to strengthen the systems of the CDTY to ensure more
sustainable organisational capacity for effective programmes delivery in future. The proposed intervention will build on the
existing emergency programme run by CAFOD and CDTY which was supported through the Caritas Internationalis Appeal
EA30 2009 and received ECHO funding (ECHO/SDN/BUD/2009/01061) for the watsan component. The wider emergency
response programme has already received funding support from the Caritas Network, Spanish Government, UNCIEF and
WFP.</narrative>
  </description>
